ded, same net assignments as before by function. Pin numbering follows XKNANO-113's real pad numbers pin-for-pin (1 VCC / 2 RST / 3 CLK / 4 CD / 5 GND / 6 VPP / 7 IO / 8 SHELL, per the manufacturer's own pin table + easyeda2kicad symbol pull); the old CD1/CD2 naming is retired since XKNANO-113's CD switch shares its return path with the socket's own GND contact (pad 5) rather than using a second dedicated pad -- old CD1 (always wired to GND) is now literally just the GND pin. VPP (pad 6) is unused by this design (ISO 7816 VPP is obsolete on modern SIM cards, matching the old part's omission of it) and is left NC. SHELL (pad 8) is grounded, standard practice for a card-edge connector's metal shield -- reuses the schematic slot the old symbol's CD1/GND pin already occupied, so no new GND wiring was needed for it either." (at 0 0 0) (show_name no) (do_not_autoplace no) (hide yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))) (property "ki_keywords" "SIM nanoSIM UICC push-push connector XKB XKNANO-113" (at 0 0 0) (show_name no) (do_not_autoplace no) (hide yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))) (property "ki_fp_filters" "*NanoSIM*" (at 0 0 0) (show_name no) (do_not_autoplace no) (hide yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))) (symbol "XKB_XKNANO-113_0_1" (rectangle (start -10.16 10.16) (end 15.24 -12.7) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type background))) (rectangle (start -1.27 3.81) (end 3.81 5.08) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type outline))) (rectangle (start -1.27 -1.27) (end 3.81 0) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type outline)))) (symbol "XKB_XKNANO-113_1_1" (pin passive line (at -12.7 7.62 0) (length 2.54) (name "VCC" (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)))) (number "1" (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016))))) (pin passive line (at -12.7 5.08 0) (length 2.54) (name "RST" (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)))) (number "2" (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016))))) (pin passive line (at -12.7 2.54 0) (length 2.54) (name "CLK" (effects (font (size 1.016